Separate input validity origin authority and truth (@computing-trust-provenance: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Account-for-data-purpose-exposure-retention-and-recovery-together.lingua#r_009E3580D265E2CF048AF92903") { r_00A3852C60830A63E0B4F976AA
A piece of input can be syntactically valid, come from an authenticated sender, and still be wrong for the intended task. These are different claims. A range check proves only the declared constraint. An authenticated message binds bytes to an actor under an authentication model. Permission allows an operation. Neither proves that the actor counted the right physical pieces or chose the intended ledger. Reuse [Specify inputs, results and failure before implementing](Specify-inputs-results-and-failure-before-implementing.lingua#r_0F6547BECCF6CA21F43948497D), [Specify one outstanding operation and a retained durable result](Specify-one-outstanding-operation-and-a-retained-durable-result.lingua#r_00529B7EA6239E5D1C8E61D93C) and [Review reporting criticism and the limits of reproduced evidence](../../inquiry/core/Review-reporting-criticism-and-the-limits-of-reproduced-evidence.lingua#r_00938E8A05E83C0B28227241FA).

In the proposed review screen, the person sees alpha and amount two. On submit, the client retains those arguments with identity one. Rendering a different object label while sending beta would violate the interaction contract even if both ledgers accepted additions. Reading the value again from an editable field on retry could similarly substitute amount three. Preserve the reviewed operation as a value; make edits explicit new proposals, and do not reuse a committed identity with changed meaning. The finite model fixes alpha and two precisely to make the retained-intent invariant small enough to inspect exhaustively; general editable drafts need their own implementation and checks.

Consider an imported list headed accepted pieces. Before submission, ask who produced it, what accepted means, what interval it covers, what unit each number uses, and whether entries have already been recorded. A cryptographic signature could support origin and integrity under its assumptions but would not answer those domain questions. The present model assumes authentic replies; it does not implement signatures or keys. A reply with the expected identity but an invented total would defeat a client that relied only on identity equality outside that assumption.

Trust boundaries also concern interpretation. A note supplied by a participant is data, not authority to change permissions or executable instructions. A display implementation must handle such text in the appropriate data channel. The abstract projection later in this block does not render text, parse a network message or defend a host process. Its limited property is which known fields it returns from an internally valid row.

**Work:** build an evidence table for an imported request, a reviewed draft, a transport reply and a displayed receipt. For each, distinguish structural validity, origin, permission, semantic meaning and evidential limits. Construct one valid-but-wrong request and one authentic-but-outdated statement. Explain the extra observation required in each case. Reuse existing byte framing and representation lessons rather than treating field labels as sufficient validation.

**Continue:** [Account for data purpose exposure retention and recovery together](Account-for-data-purpose-exposure-retention-and-recovery-together.lingua#r_009E3580D265E2CF048AF92903).

**Return:** [Computing](../Computing.lingua#r_02FE84C805C79A9D396F478641).
